From ea011e526fde91486f25526da0e527a21a07b435 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 19:45:00 +0100
Subject: mm: convert __get_unmapped_area() to use vma_flags_t

Update __get_unmapped_area() to be parameterised by vma_flags_t rather
than vm_flags_t as part of the effort to move VMA flags from a system word
to a bitmap.

We cascade the changes up to arch_get_unmapped_area_topdown() and
arch_get_unmapped_area(), where, for now, we use vma_flags_to_legacy() in
order to propagate the VMA flags.

No functional change intended.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/20260711-b4-vma-flags-mm-v2-3-0fa2357d5431@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>
Reviewed-by: Lance Yang <lance.yang@linux.dev>
Reviewed-by: Zi Yan <ziy@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Vlastimil Babka (SUSE) <vbabka@kernel.org>
Cc: Baolin Wang <baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com>
Cc: Barry Song <baohua@kernel.org>
